From eae1971d613db4d7e3bade448e402a1f0a8f5db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 15:41:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 755/913] plat-stm32mp1: remove system_off_soc and
 STM32_PM_SHUTDOWN

Remove support for the proprietary "system_off_soc_mode" property in
the PWR node, as shutdown is now handled through the
"system-power-controller" property in the PMIC node for the STPMIC1
and STPMIC2 families (STPMIC1L, STPMIC2 and STPMIC2L).

Moreover, the STPMIC software switch-off can be handled by TF-A code
running in SYSRAM (BL2 for STM32MP1 or BL31 for STM32MP2), but only
when the DDR power supplies are switched off. Therefore, it does not
need to be managed in OP-TEE through a dedicated PM state anymore.

As soc mode is always STM32_PM_CSTOP_ALLOW_STANDBY_DDR_OFF, this patch
also simplify the function stm32mp1_get_lp_soc_mode()

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git d62e0c297886de3884334f2ee1151edc0e9186ee plat-stm32mp1: remove system_off_soc and STM32_PM_SHUTDOWN]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ifa257070a4b2b765704d3e027bebeef9be9fee4b
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/577550
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
